course: dictionary
lesson: 3714
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. In «Stop flexing», the girl does not mean bending anything. She means stop showing off, because flexing is also slang for showing off something, like new trainers or money.
explain: The word flex can name a bendy part of your body, or a bendy cable. To flex your arm means to bend it. A flex on the wall is an electric cable with a plug, for a lamp or kettle. Look at the other words around it to find the meaning that fits.
explain: Muscles help you flex. «Muscles can only pull, never push», so they work in pairs. When you flex your arm, the biceps shortens and bulges to bend it, and the triceps on the back pulls to straighten it again. The clues show that flex is about bending and tightening.
fact: Flex is a verb: flex, flexes, flexed, flexing.
fact: To flex means to bend a part of your body, like your arm or fingers.
fact: To flex your muscles means to tighten them so they stand out, often to show strength.
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a flex is a bendy electric cable with a plug; in US English it is called a cord.
fact: Slang «flexing» means showing off, and «weird flex» teases someone for bragging about something odd.
exercise: Anya mentions skiing, and a girl says, «Stop flexing.» What does flexing mean here? | *Showing off | Bending her knees on the slope | Getting ready to ski | Tightening a rope
exercise: Mum says, «Don't leave the flex across the floor.» What is a flex? | *A bendy electric cable with a plug | A type of trainer | A pair of muscles in the arm | A kind of kettle
exercise: Ravi says, «To flex your fingers, slowly bend them.» What does flex mean? | To sleep | To shout | *To bend | To draw
test: In «when you flex your arm, the biceps shortens and bulges», what does the biceps do? | *Shortens and bulges | Lengthens and goes flat | Sleeps | Turns into a cable
test: Which phrase means «stop showing off»? | Flex your fingers | Stop running | *Stop flexing | Stop reading
exam: A boy brags about a stick he found, and a friend says, «Weird flex, but OK.» What does she mean? | It is a compliment about his muscles | It means the stick is a cable | It means he bent the stick very well | *It teases him for bragging about something odd
